@page "/patch-notes"
@layout GameLayout
@attribute [Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization.Authorize]

@if (!Embedded)
{
    <PageTitle>Version 1.0.1 · Path of Boredom</PageTitle>
}

<main class="patch-notes @(Embedded ? "embedded" : null)">
    @if (!Embedded)
    {
        <header class="page-header">
            <a class="back-link" href="/" aria-label="Back to game" title="Back to game"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span></a>
        </header>
        <section class="page-heading">
            <p class="eyebrow">LATEST UPDATE</p>
            <h1>Patch Notes</h1>
            <p>Changes and improvements in version 1.0.1.</p>
        </section>
    }

    <article id="version-1-0-1">
        <header class="patch-heading">
            <div class="patch-meta">
                <span class="badge">VERSION 1.0.1</span>
                <span class="badge latest">LATEST UPDATE</span>
            </div>
            <h2>More room to save your journey</h2>
            <p>This update brings a redesigned main menu, easier save management, clearer mobile menus, a more compact Forge equipment view, and a more demanding campaign and Endless opening.</p>
            <div class="tags" aria-label="Update highlights">
                <span>Main menu</span><span>Save slots</span><span>Forge artwork</span><span>Mobile menus</span><span>Challenge saves</span><span>Difficulty rebalance</span><span>Sound polish</span>
            </div>
        </header>

        <nav class="contents" aria-label="Version 1.0.1 contents">
            <a href="#main-menu">Main menu</a>
            <a href="#save-slots">Save slots</a>
            <a href="#forge-artwork">Forge artwork</a>
            <a href="#mobile-menus">Mobile menus</a>
            <a href="#challenge-saves">Challenge saves</a>
            <a href="#difficulty-and-restart">Difficulty and restart</a>
            <a href="#pickup-audio">Pickup audio</a>
        </nav>

        <section class="patch-section" id="main-menu">
            <p class="eyebrow">A NEW WAY TO SET OUT</p>
            <h3>Meet the improved main menu</h3>
            <p>The refreshed menu brings Continue, Play, Load saved run, Account Progression, and Options together in one place. Open Play to start a Campaign or enter Endless when it is unlocked. New runs show class and difficulty before starting-skill choices. Account and cloud controls live under Options, and opening Patch Notes in-game keeps the current signed-in session active.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="patch-section" id="save-slots">
            <p class="eyebrow">YOUR ADVENTURE</p>
            <h3>Choose which run to continue</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Save up to five runs and choose a save when you load.</li>
                <li>Each save shows its class and run details, so it is easy to find the right adventure.</li>
                <li>Choosing a save closes the chooser and returns to that run's summary, with its continue and restart actions.</li>
                <li>Autosaves stay with the selected run, and existing saves are kept when moving to the new save system.</li>
                <li>The save chooser uses the game's dark palette and a compact landscape layout, keeping all five slots in view on phones.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="patch-section" id="forge-artwork">
            <p class="eyebrow">AT THE FORGE</p>
            <h3>Upgrade and mastery cards get artwork</h3>
            <p>Forge upgrades and masteries now have their own artwork, giving each choice more visual character as you shape your build. The Equipment tab has a compact stat preview and shorter style choices, so it fits a landscape phone without making you scroll through long synergy and relic descriptions.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="patch-section" id="mobile-menus">
            <p class="eyebrow">BUILT FOR LANDSCAPE</p>
            <h3>Skills, Forge, and Options are easier to scan</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Skills, Forge, and Options tabs now use clearer icons, stronger selected states, and phone-sized touch targets.</li>
                <li>Account and cloud controls are grouped under Options. Relic discoveries moved out of Account Progression into Options &gt; Codex; current-run relics and synergies stay with the run summary.</li>
                <li>Patch Notes opens over the main menu and its Back button sits on the right, so reading the update no longer sends you through a sign-in reset.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="patch-section" id="challenge-saves">
            <p class="eyebrow">CHALLENGE RUNS</p>
            <h3>Challenge selections save correctly</h3>
            <p>Starting a new stage challenge no longer causes the save to fail. Your selected challenge and run can be saved as expected.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="patch-section" id="difficulty-and-restart">
            <p class="eyebrow">A CLEARER, CLEANER FLOW</p>
            <h3>Difficulty, combat pressure, and restart options</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Difficulty choices are now named Easy, Medium, and Hard, with enemy health, damage, speed, wave size, and healing retuned so upgrades matter sooner.</li>
                <li>Enemies pursue faster, and Ash runners now appear in the first wave. Wisps and Spitters lead moving targets and fire faster projectiles, so constant circling is less effective; dodge their shots and use the arena to make space.</li>
                <li>Fresh Endless runs start with a partial Watchkeeper kit instead of every Forge upgrade at maximum, leaving room to grow through the early echoes.</li>
                <li>Ranking filters use the current Easy, Medium, and Hard labels. Existing scores and ranking boards are retained.</li>
                <li>The restart action has a simpler label, and its options now sit in a compact panel while the screen behind them remains blurred.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="patch-section" id="pickup-audio">
            <p class="eyebrow">A QUIETER ADVENTURE</p>
            <h3>Coin pickups no longer chime</h3>
            <p>Routine gold pickups are silent now, so repeated collection sounds do not crowd out combat. Level-ups, upgrades, victories, and improved equipment still have audio cues.</p>
        </section>
    </article>

    @if (!Embedded)
    {
        <footer>
            <span>Version 1.0.1 · Path of Boredom</span>
            <a href="/">Return to the game</a>
        </footer>
    }
</main>

@code {
    [Parameter] public bool Embedded { get; set; }
}
